DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The guest service module for PAM allows guest logins.  If successful, the
     ppaamm__gguueesstt module sets the PAM environment variable GUEST to the login
     name.  The application can check this variable using pam_getenv(3) to
     differentiate guest logins from normal logins.

     The following options may be passed to the ppaamm__gguueesstt module:

     gguueessttss=_l_i_s_t    Comma-separated list of guest account names.  The default
                    is “guest”.  A typical value for ftpd(8) would be
                    “anonymous,ftp”.

     nnooppaassss         Omits the password prompt if the target account is on the
                    list of guest accounts.

     ppaassss__aass__rruusseerr  The password typed in by the user is exported as the
                    PAM_RUSER item.  This is useful for applications like
                    ftpd(8) where guest users are encouraged to use their
                    email address as password.

     ppaassss__iiss__uusseerr   Requires the guest user to type in the guest account name
                    as password.

